 "notes": {
  "why_hand_collected": "ottawa.ca sits behind Incapsula, which answers any scripted fetch with a JavaScript challenge instead of the page - curl gets 1.1KB of challenge script whatever headers it sends - so scripts/crawl-municipal-elections.py records Ottawa as no-list-found. The list was read in a real browser instead. This is why by-zone/ exists.",
  "why_the_url_could_not_be_guessed": "The trustee list is not a named subpage. It hangs off the certified-candidates page as a query parameter, ?page=3044842, which is why every guessed path 404'd; each board then has its own child page below that.",
  "boards_in_scope": "Ottawa publishes four boards. Only the two English ones are collected: Ottawa-Carleton DSB (B66184) and Ottawa Catholic (B67180). Conseil des ecoles publiques de l'Est de l'Ontario and Conseil des ecoles catholiques du Centre-Est are French-language and out of scope by the same decision as everywhere else in this data.",
  "acclamation": "Ottawa says it in the table's caption, not on the name: an Ottawa Catholic zone is headed 'Acclaimed candidate for ... Zone 1' where a contested one reads 'Certified candidates for ...'. Five of the ten Catholic zones are acclamations; none of the twelve OCDSB zones is.",
  "withdrawn": "Ottawa gives withdrawals their own page rather than marking them inline. One is an English-board trustee - Donna Blackburn, OCDSB Zone 3, withdrawn 2026-07-06 - and she is correctly absent from the certified list collected here. The other two are French boards. Checked at https://ottawa.ca/en/city-hall/elections/candidates/certified-and-acclaimed-candidates/withdrawn-candidates",
  "zones": "OCDSB runs 12 zones and Ottawa Catholic 10, each labelled with the city wards it covers. The label is recorded as published, e.g. 'Zone 1 (Wards 5, 6, 21)'.",
  "contact": "The page gives every  candidate a telephone, email and website/social column, and prints 'Not provided' where the candidate gave none; those are recorded as empty.",
  "page_last_updated": "2026-09-04, as stated on both board pages.",
  "retrieved": "2026-09-04"
 },
